      </div>
      <div class=3D"facts">
        <span><b>=E2=89=880.2 ms</b>per question</span>
        <span><b>0</b>trained parameters</span>
        <span><b>89,528 B</b>interpreter script</span>
        <span><b>65,404 B</b>whole store, both grammars and demo corpus</sp=
an>
        <span><b>706</b>grammar words checked absent from the code</span>
      </div>
      <p class=3D"note">Task 15 is saturated by earlier neural models, so 1=
00% is not the finding. The findings are zero training data, attribution eq=
ual to gold, invariance under permutation, and a failure on task 1 that has=
 a stated cause: no rule kind maps <em>travelled to</em> onto location, and=
 the store deliberately gives recency no power to settle contradictions.</p=
>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby=3D"outline">
      <h2 id=3D"outline">Outline</h2>
      <div class=3D"outline">

        <article class=3D"part">
          <div>
            <h3><span class=3D"n">1</span>Introduction</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>An LLM-shaped interface, rebuilt without a language model=
: input words find purchase, a reply is built, and every clause of it has a=
 source.</li>
              <li>The three things it can say, shown with <em>Does Pixel ch=
ase mice?</em> and its chain <span class=3D"mono percept"><span class=3D"s"=
>pixel</span> =E2=80=94<span class=3D"v">is a</span>=E2=86=92 <span class=
=3D"o">cat</span> =E2=9F=B9 <span class=3D"s">cat</span> =E2=80=94<span cla=
ss=3D"v">chase</span>=E2=86=92 <span class=3D"o">mouse</span></span>.</li>
              <li>Why not call it a small language model: it defines no dis=
tribution over text and generates nothing.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <aside class=3D"margin"><span class=3D"chip todo">To write</span>=
Framing settled in discussion; about one page.</aside>
        </article>

        <article class=3D"part">
          <div>
            <h3><span class=3D"n">2</span>Related work</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Symbolic understanding: SHRDLU; controlled natural langua=
ges, Attempto Controlled English above all.</li>
              <li>Extraction and graphs: open information extraction; perso=
nal knowledge graphs.</li>
              <li>Reasoning: semantic networks, defeasible inheritance, def=
ault logic, truth maintenance, Belnap's four values, subjective logic.</li>
              <li>Data: self-describing formats (NetCDF, Avro), datasheets,=
 FAIR, OAIS, local-first software.</li>
              <li>Contrast: attribution and hallucination in LLM question a=
nswering; small language models.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <aside class=3D"margin"><span class=3D"chip todo">To verify</span=
>Reference list below is from memory. Check every entry, and state plainly =
how this differs from ACE.</aside>
        </article>

        <article class=3D"part">
          <div>
            <h3><span class=3D"n">3</span>The self-describing store</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>One file across the MOF layers: episodes and terms (M0), =
term and percept blocks (M1), grammar kinds (M2), the record format itself =
(M3). TBox and ABox side by side, plus weighted beliefs about the design.</=
li>
              <li>Metacircular: grammar and blueprint are records in the fo=
rmat they define.</li>
              <li>Rule of least power: the grammar can change what the inte=
rpreter says, never what it can do.</li>
              <li>Where the analogy stops: not a quine, not homoiconic; sel=
f-describing to a reader, not self-hosting.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <aside class=3D"margin"><span class=3D"chip drafted">Argument dra=
fted</span>Needs a figure: the MOF layer table beside real record IDs <code=
>@LAT-10LON0</code>, <code>@LAT85LON0</code>, <code>@LAT90LON5</code>.</asi=
de>
        </article>

        <article class=3D"part">
          <div>
            <h3><span class=3D"n">4</span>From words to beliefs</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Reading, classification, and the percept line <span class=
=3D"mono percept">sentence | <span class=3D"s">subject</span> | <span class=
=3D"v">vector</span> | <span class=3D"o">object</span> | =C2=B1 | quantifie=
r</span>.</li>
              <li>Consolidation over episodes, not sentences:</li>
            </ul>
            <p class=3D"formula">conf =3D round(255 =C2=B7 (max(for, agains=
t) + 1) / (for + against + 2))</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Verdicts as Belnap's values: Yes =E2=86=92 true, No =E2=
=86=92 false, Contested =E2=86=92 both, Unknown =E2=86=92 neither.</li>
              <li>Reasoning order: said, transitive, inverse or symmetric, =
inherited from the nearest IS-A ancestor; specificity overrides, and an ove=
rruled ancestor is reported.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <aside class=3D"margin"><span class=3D"chip ready">Evidence in re=
po</span><code>TTG-RFC-0002</code>, <code>TTG-RFC-0003</code>, blueprint re=
cords <code>@LAT10LON0</code>=E2=80=93<code>@LAT70LON0</code>. Compress; do=
n't re-derive.</aside>
        </article>

        <article class=3D"part">
          <div>
            <h3><span class=3D"n">5</span>Two languages, one algebra</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Membership by <code>lang:</code>; later languages borrow =
numbers and vector algebra and add only labels and phrases.</li>
              <li>Per-sentence choice by recognised function words, seed ve=
rbs and irregular forms; replies in the question's language, quotes in the =
speaker's.</li>
              <li>Negative result: one merged lexicon breaks 2 of 15 Englis=
h parses (<em>a</em>, <em>no</em>).</li>
              <li>What does not cross: content words until linked, verbs no=
t at all.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <aside class=3D"margin"><span class=3D"chip ready">Evidence in re=
po</span><code>TTG-RFC-0001 =C2=A711</code>, belief <code>@LAT98LON7</code>=
, suite section =E2=80=9Ctwo languages, one sphere=E2=80=9D.</aside>
        </article>

        <article class=3D"part">
          <div>
            <h3><span class=3D"n">6</span>Evaluation</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>6.1 Substitution.</strong> Delete the grammar; ad=
d Spanish; the leak check over 706 words.</li>
              <li><strong>6.2 bAbI.</strong> Tasks 15 and 1, both splits, w=
ith the permutation test and its control.</li>
              <li><strong>6.3 A small-LM baseline.</strong> One or two 1=E2=
=80=933B models on the same stories: accuracy, whether cited sentences matc=
h gold, latency, determinism.</li>
              <li><strong>6.4 Coverage on real notes.</strong> Share of sen=
tences yielding a percept, and percept precision on a few hundred hand-labe=
lled sentences.</li>
              <li><strong>6.5 Rebuilding from the store.</strong> A third p=
arty's report of what the store alone let an agent build; make it systemati=
c.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <aside class=3D"margin"><span class=3D"chip ready">6.1, 6.2 done<=
/span><span class=3D"chip todo">6.3=E2=80=936.5 to do</span>6.3 is the resu=
lt reviewers will ask for first.</aside>
        </article>

        <article class=3D"part">
          <div>
            <h3><span class=3D"n">7</span>Limitations and disclosures</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Subject=E2=80=93verb=E2=80=93object only; modifiers dropp=
ed; Spanish dropped subjects, verb-first questions, adjective agreement.</l=
i>
              <li>bAbI task 15 uses two sentence templates, and its README =
asks for no task-specific tricks: the phrase line is one, declared.</li>
              <li>The phrase was chosen after reading one test story; the t=
rain split gives the same result.</li>
              <li>Two language-independent question rules were added to the=
 interpreter during this evaluation (stranded preposition; copula before a =
declared phrase), each with regression tests on non-bAbI sentences.</li>
              <li>No recency: a change of mind reads as a contradiction, by=
 design.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <aside class=3D"margin"><span class=3D"chip drafted">List ready</=
span>Honesty here is what makes 100% believable.</aside>
        </article>

        <article class=3D"part">
          <div>
            <h3><span class=3D"n">8</span>Conclusion and future work</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>bAbI ships task 15 in Hindi: a third grammar, and the fir=
st subject=E2=80=93object=E2=80=93verb one.</li>
              <li>RuleTaker and ProofWriter, whose closed- and open-world s=
ettings include an <em>unknown</em> answer.</li>
              <li>A rule kind for verb entailment (<em>moves to</em> =E2=9F=
=B9 <em>in</em>), and linking vectors across languages.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <aside class=3D"margin"><span class=3D"chip todo">To write</span>=
Half a page.</aside>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

